# System localisation

UI strings live in `packages/system/lang/{en,ru}.json`. Content translations are Forge/SQLite
— see `docs/forge/localisation.md`. Do not mix them.

## Hard rules

- **No hard-coded user-facing English** in `.ts` or `.hbs`. Use `game.i18n.localize` /
  `format`, or the Handlebars `localize` helper, with a `KEDOM.…` (or Foundry `TYPES.…`) key.
- **Add the key to both `en.json` and `ru.json` in the same change.** English is canonical;
  Russian is required for system UI, not optional.
- **Never duplicate a JSON object key** (e.g. two `"Sheet"` siblings). The later one silently
  wins and drops the earlier labels.
- **Keys are identity.** Prefer `KEDOM.Chat.UnknownSkill`, not concatenating display words.

## Config-driven labels

When a key is built from a closed enum (`ABILITY_KEYS`, `SKILL_KEYS`, `PROFICIENCY_TIERS`,
outcomes), every enum member must have a leaf string. If you introduce a new
`` `KEDOM.Foo.${x}` `` pattern, add an expander in
`packages/system/src/i18n/collect-lang-refs.ts`.

## Gate

`packages/system/src/i18n/lang-keys.test.ts` (via `npm test`) fails when a referenced key is
missing or empty in en/ru, when en/ru key sets diverge, or when a template key has no
expander. Run it after adding strings; do not skip it.
